! Step 16 hand-back

Head `19048159c1c5beec52f72c049e5c53dc20cb6779`; no live seats; no push; no commit. The state counter stays 16. ''Broker liveness wall:'' request 031's `node tools/wait-receipt.mjs` returned `receipt-timeout: res-031.json absent or incomplete after 120000ms; broker may have died`. Its execution and eventual result remain unknown; resolve that request before issuing another, and do not assume the broker accepted or finished it. Next unused request 032.

Two uncommitted files carry the bounded work: `packages/lararium-node/src/edge-shadow-ring.ts` and `packages/lararium-node/tests/edge-shadow-ring.test.ts`. The test extends the existing clean-board control to demand a synchronous invalidation when a followed board moves, before its asynchronous refold notification. Relay 030 returned the intended red: 14 pass, 1 fail at the new invalidation assertion. The implementation adds optional `onInvalidate` immediately after the reading goes dark and its refold is queued. `git diff --check` passed. Relay 031 requested the same single-file green run but timed out awaiting a receipt; ''green remains unverified''. No consumer connects the new callback yet.

The ring callback by itself cannot fence cross-worker proof changes: the daemon's face seat reads its own board through `boardDyadReader`, while the node ring lives on the vessel side. Both invalidation and a wake after the authoritative refold need lifecycle-safe transport or a proven equivalent local subscription; test movement during refold and initial attachment races on node and browser. Existing `onRefold` currently fires even when refold rejects (the catch precedes the callback), so a consumer must not mistake that signal alone for a successfully published fold. A movement during ingest needs more than a post-await version test: `absorbCapEvents` invokes `kh.ingestPeerEvents`, then settles and persists; those operations can mutate authority before returning. Establish and test a guarded or serialized commit boundary before claiming that race closed.

All remaining work from step 15 stays owed: founder lineage freshness, tri-state ring, remaining blind-read residues and daemon join TOCTOU; a complete-view dyad census with independently supported completeness (the fleet board has no roster); `runApplyAdmitPayload`, holder-session-proof and leaf-peer-proof authority readers. Keep roll guard and epoch fields until later slices. Whole non-daemon suites remain due before ready; daemon suites run named single files through the broker. E2e stays in CI. Obtain blind Opus custody read before land; no push without controller go.

<<~/ahu>>

